<<~ ahu #/entry>>
! Geometry speaks in several tongues

A pet-named location holds an ecology of anonymous entities and independently
validated representations. CAD rules testify to measurable material joins,
polygon surfaces give sculptural form, heightfields and point sets give measured
evidence, and signed distance fields MAY propose caves, fractures and erosion.
No representation's capabilities automatically transfer to another kernel.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/invariants>>
!! Identity, relation, and kernel authority

* ''Identity enacts Relation.'' Bind each sculptural or physical entity to
  named anchors, capability descriptors, source receipts, and a location frame.
  An OpenCascade face number or a polygon vertex number alone never holds a
  long-lived pet-name.
* ''Structural truth stays local.'' A certified BRep union belongs to its CAD
  body. A watertight polymesh with positive volume earns a render/surface
  claim, not an exact STEP certificate. A measured point cloud carries testimony,
  not a generator of hidden chambers.
* ''Attachment makes a testable promise.'' The CAD cage and mesh share
  position through explicit vertices and CAD shape anchors, with recorded
  distances and tolerance. Contact-proximity does not prove strength or
  mechanical fusion.
* ''Composition does not coerce union.'' A combined render MAY include CAD,
  polymesh, SDF and observed sources, but it MUST name the producer and audit
  for each. Only a tested and explicit conversion/Boolean may upgrade authority.
* ''The grammar may surprise us.'' An unnamed polygon branch MAY deform
  beyond the initial BRep's appearance, yet must not destroy the unchanged
  structural cage without renewed validation. Pet-naming and o-takiage remain
  soft generational relationships, not topological traps.
* ''Every method retains provenance.'' A triangulated witness, an authored
  OpenSCAD grammar, or a surveyed DEM each retains its own source digest,
  units, transform, license and uncertainty. Neither CGI nor synthetic source
  alignment confers independent real-world registration.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/implementation>>
!! Executable and prospective capability stacks

`tools/projection-loom/projection_loom/hybrid.py` composes a validated CAD
assembly, polygon layers and explicit anchors. `examples/necrospire/hybrid/`
keeps a procedural faceted crystal distinct from the castle's BRep STEP.
The two-epoch benchmark deliberately records whether the added polygon layer
helps or hurts source agreement. OpenVDB/SDF backends, automatic BRep conversion
and native OpenUSD stage export remain prospective, not implemented claims.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/evergreen-capability-composition>>

!! CAD-derived mesh recipes enter the active OODA-HA helm

The crystal mesh now grows from its validated CAD seed. A versioned recipe holds CAD/mesh loci, optional Joining skin, protected semantic socket and original source digest. Each capability executes in a child OODA-HA loop within the same Candidate Act and returns only its own scoped geometric authority. The old two-epoch hybrid script serves as historical comparison, never as a competing scheduler.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>
